// v3.0.0 (3d no_std): panic_handler M0 stub.
//
// This is the minimum freestanding panic handler. When the no_std entry
// point (`__start_kernel`) or user code calls panic, control transfers
// here. Per `jhyy-lang-spec-no_std-supplement-v3.0.0.md`, panic semantics
// are: stop the kernel (no unwind, no message in M0). A real panic message
// printer lands in a later v3.x sprint.
//
// jhyy has no `!` (never) type nor explicit `()` unit return per lang-spec
// §3 / §8.3 — void functions simply omit the `-> T` clause. The body is an
// infinite loop — divergence is correct (function never returns). A future
// backend can lower this to `ud2` / `hlt`.
fn panic_handler() {
    while true {
    }
}
